 "title": "Social capital",
 "hook": "Using data on billions of Facebook connections and group memberships, Raj Chetty et al.’s Social Capital Atlas calculates three metrics for US counties, ZIP codes, high schools, and colleges: economic connectedness (friendships between low-income and high-income users), cohesiveness (how often users’ friends are also friends with one another), and civic engagement (membership in volunteer groups).",
